the markdown feature description file to \\\\`ready\\\\`\\n6. Finally, print a 1 or 2 sentence commit statement for git. No need to do anything else for git, no need to commit.\\n\\nYou may read any files referenced by relative paths in the spec and any file you think is related to the spec.\\nRespect the Test Plan and Acceptance Criteria. Keep everything short and to the point.\\n\\nBe brief, but never compress away the subject, timing, or causal chain. Define ambiguous technical phrases. use $caveman skill\"\n.\\design\\actions\\fix bug.md:6:Use the Block Workflow:\r\n.\\design\\actions\\fix bug.md:8:1. Propose a Change Plan with blocks (no edits yet).\r\n.\\design\\activity\\card__012efbb1-c938-4539-a646-0f263e72dea6.json:11:          \"content\": \"Read and implement the feature/job described in:  `C:\\\\Users\\\\janbo\\\\Documents\\\\dev\\\\md2\\\\design/feature_descriptions/F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md`\\n\\nYou do not need to look at the git status. This is not your concern.  The worktree is what it is, you only need to touch what is required for the above mentioned job/feature description.\\n\\nUse the Block Workflow:\\n\\n1. Propose a Change Plan with blocks (no edits yet).\\n2. create a task for each block\\n3. Wait for approval.\\n4. include tests.\\n5. After implementation is done, update the field `status` in the markdown feature description file to \\\\`ready\\\\`. Be carefully, you are working in `C:\\\\Users\\\\janbo\\\\Documents\\\\dev\\\\md2`, the file to update is at `C:\\\\Users\\\\janbo\\\\Documents\\\\dev\\\\md2\\\\design/feature_descriptions/F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md`\\n\\nYou may read any files referenced by relative paths in the spec and any file you think is related to the spec.\\nRespect the Test Plan and Acceptance Criteria.&#x20;\\n\\nYou should only run the related tests, do not run the entire test suite, that will be done manually later on.\\n\\nBe brief, but never compress away the subject, timing, or causal chain. Define ambiguous technical phrases. use $caveman skill\",\n.\\design\\activity\\card__012efbb1-c938-4539-a646-0f263e72dea6.json:583:          \"content\": \"Change Plan created. No edits made.\\n\\n1. Block 1 — Chat reservation\\n\\n   Add invisible event-sized slots to `ActionConversationChat`.\\n\\n   - Running block: visible event with `started`, `inProgress`, or `running` status.\\n   - Permanent block: message, completed tool group, or terminal event.\\n   - Active chat keeps minimum one reserved slot.\\n   - Running blocks replace slots.\\n   - Disappearing running blocks restore same slot count.\\n   - New permanent blocks reduce surplus slots until one remains.\\n   - Reset tracking when conversation changes or run stops.\\n\\n2. Block 2 — Tests\\n\\n   Add focused tests covering baseline, one/multiple running blocks, disappearance, permanent-block reduction, inactive runs, conversation changes, grouping, and sticky scrolling.\\n\\n3. Block 3 — Verification and status\\n\\n   Run affected conversation tests and lint touched files only. Fix related failures. Set [F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/design/feature_descriptions/F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md) `status: ready`.\\n\\nApprove plan to start edits.\\n\\n\",\n.\\design\\activity\\card__012efbb1-c938-4539-a646-0f263e72dea6.json:612:          \"content\": \"Read and implement the feature/job described in:  `C:\\\\Users\\\\janbo\\\\Documents\\\\dev\\\\md2\\\\design/feature_descriptions/F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md`\\n\\nYou do not need to look at the git status. This is not your concern.  The worktree is what it is, you only need to touch what is required for the above mentioned job/feature description.\\n\\nUse the Block Workflow:\\n\\n1. Propose a Change Plan with blocks (no edits yet).\\n2. create a task for each block\\n3. Wait for approval.\\n4. include tests.\\n5. After implementation is done, update the field `status` in the markdown feature description file to \\\\`ready\\\\`. Be carefully, you are working in `C:\\\\Users\\\\janbo\\\\Documents\\\\dev\\\\md2`, the file to update is at `C:\\\\Users\\\\janbo\\\\Documents\\\\dev\\\\md2\\\\design/feature_descriptions/F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md`\\n\\nYou may read any files referenced by relative paths in the spec and any file you think is related to the spec.\\nRespect the Test Plan and Acceptance Criteria.&#x20;\\n\\nYou should only run the related tests, do not run the entire test suite, that will be done manually later on.\\n\\nBe brief, but never compress away the subject, timing, or causal chain. Define ambiguous technical phrases. use $caveman skill\",\n.\\design\\activity\\card__012efbb1-c938-4539-a646-0f263e72dea6.json:1423:          \"content\": \"desktop\\\\test_agent_spawn.mjs:18:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"turn.completed\\\",\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":15514,\\\"cached_input_tokens\\\":9984,\\\"output_tokens\\\":7,\\\"reasoning_output_tokens\\\":0}}\\ndesign\\\\communications\\\\peerlist post.md:14:* Implement the card by running the `implement` prompt in the context of that worktree.\\ndesign\\\\communications\\\\peerlist post.md:15:* Verify the implementation manually, usually by reviewing the diff, or by running the `verify implementation` prompt.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\activity\\\\card__56dd54b0-9554-4545-85d4-bb45efef4d6e.json:17:            \\\"design/feature_descriptions/B_85_add_the_reference_to_a_chatlog_to_a_card_as_soon_as_possible.md\\\"\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F-6-animations.md:15:Use animations to indicate that long running actions are busy when the duration is unknown.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\B_107_websocket_agent_selection.md:17:Also, the project config for the default agent settings is not shared over websocket, so on the action popup, the wrong agent settings are always used initially.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\B_107_websocket_agent_selection.md:34:- On disconnect or failed initial load, mark remote desktop config unavailable. Keep agent controls disabled until host config and availability finish loading; report load or save failure through `dialogService` rather than running with browser defaults.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\B_107_websocket_agent_selection.md:40:- After WebSocket connection, action popups initially show host desktop defaults for agent, model, permission mode, and thinking level.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_147_live_update_token_usage_action_popup.md:5:title: Live update token usage action popup\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_147_live_update_token_usage_action_popup.md:14:To investigate: i think token count on action popup is only at end of conversation updated. I think we can do better\\ndesktop\\\\src\\\\shell\\\\update_service.js:157: * Errors are swallowed so a failed download leaves the running app untouched.\\ndesktop\\\\src\\\\shell\\\\update_service.js:174:        // Download/launch failures are non-fatal; keep the current app running.\\ndesign\\\\CODEMAP.md:70:- `remote` → [app/src/services/data/remote_control_storage_service.ts](../app/src/services/data/remote_control_storage_service.ts). A WebSocket client that re-implements the same bridge RPC over WS to a desktop running the remote-control server. Used when the renderer runs in a phone browser.\\ndesign\\\\CODEMAP.md:84:- Central store: [app/src/services/data/data_service.ts](../app/src/services/data/data_service.ts) owns `DataServiceState` (project, snapshot, running agents, save state). Delegates to collaborators: `ProjectState`, `ProjectLoading`, `CardOperations`, `AgentIntegration`, `ReleaseOperations`, `SaveStateService` (all in `services/project/` and `services/data/`).\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_131_add_tooltip_to_model_setup.md:14:in the action popup and app bar, we have a set of dropdowns to set up the model and related security. add tooltips to all dropdowns so it is clear what they are for.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_122_show_conversation_context_window_usage.md:15:Show the percentage of the selected conversation's context window that is used in the action popup, beside the existing total-token usage at the left of the bottom action row.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_122_show_conversation_context_window_usage.md:21:`ActionUsageSummary` displays aggregate token usage for the action and card in `ActionPopupBottomRow`. The popup already exposes `controller.displayedConversation`, but the summary does not receive it.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_126_bottom_of_action_popup_not_visible.md:5:title: Bottom of action popup not visible\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_126_bottom_of_action_popup_not_visible.md:14:On mobile, when action popup fully expanded, the bottom bar is not visible. It is hidden behind android buttons. We should leave some space\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_169_send_btn_small_screen_action_popup.md:5:title: Send btn Small screen action popup\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_169_send_btn_small_screen_action_popup.md:14:When the screen is small, like mobile, on the action popup, the buttons on the bottom row are not visible. The screen is too narrow. When flip phone horizontal, buttons are there. I think problem is only 2 places in grid. Should be flex like on normal width.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_169_send_btn_small_screen_action_popup.md:16:To make more room for the buttons at the bottom of the action popup, when in small screen, use l, m, h, instead of low medium high. Also when narrow, the middle section (tokens, changes, lines) should shrink. Drop labels. Use style and colors.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_169_send_btn_small_screen_action_popup.md:20:`ActionPopupFrame` makes the popup full-screen below the `md` breakpoint. `ActionPopupBottomRow` places agent selectors, usage, and action buttons in one flex row, but gives the first two groups fixed minimum widths of 158 px and 235 px. It also declares itself as an inline-size query container while trying to query its own width; a CSS container query only matches descendants of a container, not the container itself. No ancestor query container exists in this popup path, so its intended `<= 420px` two-column grid never activates. Fixed widths can then push Schedule, Send, Run, Stop, or Finish outside a portrait viewport.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_169_send_btn_small_screen_action_popup.md:26:* Define **narrow** as an action-popup footer width of 420 px or less. Add an outer inline-size container in `ActionPopupBottomRow`, then apply its container query to an inner layout row so the query measures the popup rather than the viewport.\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\current_data_model.md:17:| Card popover | [card_body_popover.tsx](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/components/card_view/card_body_popover.tsx:56) | Associates dirty state, title drafts, running actions, deletion, and navigation with `card.path`. |\\r\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\current_data_model.md:26:| Conversations | [action_conversation_picker.tsx](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/components/actions/action_conversation_picker.tsx:36), `ActionPopupContent`, `useActionPopupController` | Conversation records are selected by compound activity reference; card ownership uses stable `cardInternalId`. |\\r\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\current_data_model.md:68:Electron retains some transient state—current project, running executions, locks, schedules, watchers—but not the renderer’s complete card snapshot.\\r\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_162_more_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:5:title: more improve bottom buttons row on action popup\\ndesktop\\\\src\\\\shell\\\\preload.test.mjs:182:        listener({ sender: 'internal' }, { endpoint: 'ws://localhost:3555', running: true });\\ndesktop\\\\src\\\\shell\\\\preload.test.mjs:186:        expect(callback).toHaveBeenCalledWith({ endpoint: 'ws://localhost:3555', running: true });\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md:5:title: Bottom of chatlog\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md:15:On the action popup, when the agent is running. We get a lot of 'reasoning' boxes which disapear when done. There are also lots of toolcalls which combine into 1 box. This results in the bottom of the chatlog that continuously jumps: boxes popup and go away making the whole chatlog move.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md:17:Instead it would be better to keep a spot reserved for when there is nothing in a state of ´running´. Once something pops up, we remove the placeholder.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_170_bottom_of_chatlog.md:19:If there are multiple ´running´ blocks, reserve equal amount of reserved blocks and show them when the disapear. When a perminent block appears, we can decrease the reserved blocks count until back to 1.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_107_steering_prompts_disappear.md:14:When an agent is running and we send a steering prompt to it, the prompt just disappears until the backend reports back that it has been sent. this is super annoying.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_107_steering_prompts_disappear.md:16:instead, we should put it in a wait queue, shown visually on the ui by already adding the prompt to the chatlog, but in a 'in transit' state, with a button to 'steer' which should send it immediately.  Otherwise, the prompt will be sent after the next waitforInput state\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:135:        class ActionPopup\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:136:        class ActionPopupContent\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:291:    DataService --> AgentConversationService : reads running agents\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:381:    AgentChatFab --> ActionPopup\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:410:    ActionEntryPoints --> ActionPopup\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:411:    CardRunButton --> ActionPopup\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:412:    ActionPopup --> ActionPopupContent\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:413:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionAgentForm\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:414:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionConversationChat\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:415:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionConversationPicker\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:416:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionPhraseButtons\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:417:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionRunHistory\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:418:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionRunStatus\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:419:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionScheduleForm\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:420:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionSelector\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:421:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionUsageSummary\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:422:    ActionPopupContent --> ResizablePopper\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:429:    ActionPopup --> ActionExecutionService : reads live execution\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:457:    TextView --> ActionPopup\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\class_relationships.md:532:    SearchControl --> ActionPopup\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:5:title: no prefill prompt running conv\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:10:>>>>>>> f_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:21:When an agent is waiting for a response, but the action popup was closed or on the wrong 'action', then when the user clicks on the action to view the conversation and answer, the input box is prefilled again with the action's prompt. this is annoying cause it needs to be removed.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:23:so, when activating an action that has a running conversation, don't prefill the input\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:27:`useActionPopupController` prepares an action's stored prompt for a new conversation. When popup opens on another action, or reopens while execution state is being restored, that prepared prompt can remain in `promptState` when user selects action with a `queued`, `running`, or `waitingForInput` conversation.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_93_action_popup_finish_button_disabled.md:5:title: action popup finish button disabled\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_93_action_popup_finish_button_disabled.md:13:The 'finish' button on the action popup should remain disabled while the agent is still rendering output and not waiting for a response.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_152_open_github_repository_from_electron.md:13:When the react app is running in the electron environment, it defaults to opening projects by selecting a folder.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_152_open_github_repository_from_electron.md:20:We need to add an 'open dialog' to support this feature. from this dialog, the user can always choose between personal or public repository, and when running in the electron environment, the user can also select a folder.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:15:when you close and re-open an action popup, the selected agent configuration is lost and appears to go back to default.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:19:`ActionPopupContent` creates a new `ActionRunInputStore` for each action/context mount. Selector changes update that store, but closing the popup destroys it. Reopening creates an empty snapshot, so `useActionRunSettings` resolves agent, model, thinking level, access level, and approval policy from the action definition and desktop defaults again.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:46:* Project, folder, and regular-file action popups keep current session-only selector behavior.\\napp\\\\src\\\\theme\\\\theme_provider.tsx:18: * Electron main process when running on the desktop.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\B_100_claude_agent_shows_all_responses_double.md:13:When an action is run by the claude agent, all responses, accept the last one he gives are shown 2 times in the chatlog. so 2 identical bubbles below each other.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\B_100_claude_agent_shows_all_responses_double.md:42:* Running a Claude action produces exactly one chatlog bubble per assistant step; no step (except formerly the last) is duplicated.\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\initial description\\\\animations.md:6:to indicate that long running actions are busy (and we don't know how long they will run), animations can be used.\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\initial description\\\\action_popup.md:13:- While the action is running, `Cancel` asks Electron to stop the active process and chain.\\ndesign\\\\architecture\\\\initial description\\\\actions.md:74:- Activating an entry point opens the action popup for the action `id` and selected context.\\ndesign\\\\actions\\\\prepare-project.json:10:  \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"Your task is to prepare this project for development.\\\\n\\\\nInstructions:\\\\n\\\\n1. Start by locating and reading the \\\\\\\\`README.md\\\\\\\\` file in the current directory.\\\\n2. Follow the setup instructions in that README exactly.\\\\n3. If the main README refers to additional \\\\\\\\`README.md\\\\\\\\` files in subdirectories, or if subdirectories contain setup instructions that are required for development, read those as well.\\\\n4. Perform all necessary project setup steps, including (where applicable):\\\\n   1. Installing dependencies.\\\\n   2. Installing toolchains or SD