d system event rendering unchanged. Existing `AgentToolEvent` multiline rendering displays each diagnostic line in order.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_83_chatlog_sticky_at_end.md:5:title: chatlog sticky at end\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_83_chatlog_sticky_at_end.md:16:when chatlog is loaded, auto scroll to end, keep it sticky at end while it is at end\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_83_chatlog_sticky_at_end.md:20:`ActionPopupContent` provides the chat scroll container. `ActionConversationChat` renders the selected or live conversation, but neither component tracks whether the viewport is at the end. Loading a conversation and streaming new content therefore leave the scroll position unchanged.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_82_waitforinput_state_display.md:17:When a streaming-agent goes into 'WaitForInput' state, the card action button and buttons on the action popup should no longer show 'running' state, but 'waitForInput' state so that the user knows he needs to look at the card.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_82_waitforinput_state_display.md:21:`waitingForInput` already exists in desktop execution events, renderer execution state, and persisted agent conversations. `CardRunButton` recognizes waiting conversations and shows a warning-colored outline and help icon without its running spinner.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_82_waitforinput_state_display.md:23:Live card state can still appear as running until conversation data refreshes because the button does not read `runningExecution.status`. `ActionPopup` reduces all active executions to `runningActionIds`; `ActionSelector` therefore shows a primary-colored running spinner and “Agent is running” for waiting actions.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_82_waitforinput_state_display.md:29:- Pass each active root action's status from `ActionPopup` to `ActionSelector` instead of only running ids.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_3\\\\F_82_waitforinput_state_display.md:30:- Render waiting buttons